.SH hee-shell(1)
.PP
hee-shell \[en] ssh into a known TCOS host by short alias.
.PP
Real, deliberately thin: this is \f[V]ssh\f[R] with TCOS\[cq]s own host
aliases baked in, not a new protocol or a permissions mechanism.
It cannot grant access a key doesn\[cq]t already have \[en] if the
calling session\[cq]s key isn\[cq]t authorized on the target
host/account, this fails exactly like a bare \f[V]ssh\f[R] call would,
with the same real error.
.PP
Alias table only includes hosts actually confirmed reachable by name
this session \[en] not speculative.
Add more here as they\[cq]re verified, not guessed.
.PP
usage: hee-shell <alias|host> [user]
.PP
